Below is a Java program that converts XML to JSON. The program uses the `javax.xml.parsers` package for XML parsing and the `org.json` library for JSON generation.

**Java Program: XML to JSON Converter**

```java
import javax.xml.parsers.DocumentBuilderFactory;
import javax.xml.parsers.DocumentBuilder;
import org.w3c.dom.Document;
import org.w3c.dom.NodeList;
import org.w3c.dom.Node;
import org.w3c.dom.Element;
import org.json.JSONObject;
import org.json.JSONArray;
import java.io.File;

public class XmlToJsonConverter {

    public static JSONObject convertXmlToJson(File xmlFile) throws Exception {
        DocumentBuilderFactory factory = DocumentBuilderFactory.newInstance();
        DocumentBuilder builder = factory.newDocumentBuilder();
        Document document = builder.parse(xmlFile);
        document.getDocumentElement().normalize();

        return convertElementToJson(document.getDocumentElement());
    }

    private static JSONObject convertElementToJson(Element element) {
        JSONObject json = new JSONObject();

        // Process attributes
        if (element.hasAttributes()) {
            JSONObject attributes = new JSONObject();
            for (int i = 0; i < element.getAttributes().getLength(); i++) {
                Node attribute = element.getAttributes().item(i);
                attributes.put("@" + attribute.getNodeName(), attribute.getNodeValue());
            }
            json.put("attributes", attributes);
        }

        // Process child elements
        NodeList nodeList = element.getChildNodes();
        for (int i = 0; i < nodeList.getLength(); i++) {
            Node node = nodeList.item(i);
            if (node.getNodeType() == Node.ELEMENT_NODE) {
                Element childElement = (Element) node;
                String tagName = childElement.getTagName();

                // Handle multiple child elements with the same tag
                if (json.has(tagName)) {
                    Object existingValue = json.get(tagName);
                    if (existingValue instanceof JSONArray) {
                        ((JSONArray) existingValue).put(convertElementToJson(childElement));
                    } else {
                        JSONArray array = new JSONArray();
                        array.put(existingValue);
                        array.put(convertElementToJson(childElement));
                        json.put(tagName, array);
                    }
                } else {
                    json.put(tagName, convertElementToJson(childElement));
                }
            } else if (node.getNodeType() == Node.TEXT_NODE && !node.getTextContent().trim().isEmpty()) {
                json.put("#text", node.getTextContent().trim());
            }
        }

        // If no child elements, return text content
        if (json.isEmpty() && element.hasChildNodes()) {
            NodeList children = element.getChildNodes();
            for (int i = 0; i < children.getLength(); i++) {
                Node child = children.item(i);
                if (child.getNodeType() == Node.TEXT_NODE) {
                    return new JSONObject().put("#text", child.getTextContent().trim());
                }
            }
        }

        return json;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        try {
            File xmlFile = new File("input.xml"); // Replace with your XML file path
            JSONObject json = convertXmlToJson(xmlFile);
            System.out.println(json.toString(4)); // Pretty print JSON with 4-space indentation
        } catch (Exception e) {
            e.printStackTrace();
        }
    }
}
```

**Dependencies:**

*   **org.json**: Add the following dependency to your `pom.xml` if using Maven:
    ```xml
    <dependency>
        <groupId>org.json</groupId>
        <artifactId>json</artifactId>
        <version>20210307</version>
    </dependency>
    ```

**Usage:**

1.  Save the XML file you want to convert as `input.xml` in the same directory as the Java program.
2.  Run the `XmlToJsonConverter` class.
3.  The program will output the JSON representation of the XML file to the console.

**Example XML Input (`input.xml`):**

```xml
<employee id="123">
    <name>John Doe</name>
    <role>Software Engineer</role>
    <skills>
        <skill>Java</skill>
        <skill>XML</skill>
        <skill>JSON</skill>
    </skills>
</employee>
```

**Example JSON Output:**

```json
{
    "employee": {
        "attributes": {
            "@id": "123"
        },
        "name": {
            "#text": "John Doe"
        },
        "role": {
            "#text": "Software Engineer"
        },
        "skills": {
            "skill": [
                {
                    "#text": "Java"
                },
                {
                    "#text": "XML"
                },
                {
                    "#text": "JSON"
                }
            ]
        }
    }
}
```

This program provides a basic XML to JSON conversion, handling elements, attributes, and text content. You can modify it to suit your specific XML structure and requirements.
